                <pb facs="0933" n="926" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.9415 Amur River/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-03T11:00:00+09:00">July 3, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 3—1:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. My 174, July 2, 2 p.m. A press dispatch from Moscow reports that Shigemitsu
                    announced on July 2 that the Soviet Government consented to withdraw its forces
                    from the occupied Amur River islands and to return to their stations the Soviet
                    gunboats concentrated in that vicinity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
